ng with '```', else you will fail.\n2. Use only variables that you have defined!\n3. Always use the right arguments for the tools. DO NOT pass the arguments as a dict as in 'answer = wikipedia_search({'query': \"What is the place where James Bond lives?\"})', but use the arguments directly as in 'answer = wikipedia_search(query=\"What is the place where James Bond lives?\")'.\n4. For tools WITHOUT JSON output schema: Take care to not chain too many sequential tool calls in the same code block, as their output format is unpredictable. For instance, a call to wikipedia_search without a JSON output schema has an unpredictable return format, so do not have another tool call that depends on its output in the same block: rather output results with print() to use them in the next block.\n5. For tools WITH JSON output schema: You can confidently chain multiple tool calls and directly access structured output fields in the same code block! When a tool has a JSON output schema, you know exactly what fields and data types to expect, allowing you to write robust code that directly accesses the structured response (e.g., result['field_name']) without needing intermediate print() statements.\n6. Call a tool only when needed, and never re-do a tool call that you previously did with the exact same parameters.\n7. Don't name any new variable with the same name as a tool: for instance don't name a variable 'final_answer'.\n8. Never create any notional variables in our code, as having these in your logs will derail you from the true variables.\n9. You can use imports in your code, but only from the following list of modules: ['collections', 'datetime', 'itertools', 'json', 'math', 'queue', 'random', 're', 'stat', 'statistics', 'time', 'unicodedata']\n10. The state persists between code executions: so if in one step you've created variables or imported modules, these will all persist.\n11. Don't give up! You're in charge of solving the task, not providing directions to solve it.\n\nNow Begin!"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\n# Unicode word frequencies\n\nOnly modify `words.py`. Implement `word_counts(text: str) -> list[tuple[str,int]]`.\nUse Unicode character categories (unicodedata.category): a word starts with a\nletter (category L*) or number (N*) and continues across letters, numbers and\ncombining marks (M*). A mark without an active word is ignored. Any other\ncharacter ends the current word: underscore, hyphen, apostrophe, whitespace,\nsymbols and emoji are separators. Do not normalize the input before finding\nword boundaries. Thus 'a\\u0301' is one word but a leading combining mark is ignored.\n\nNormalize each completed word with NFC, then casefold, then NFC again. Count\nequal normalized words together. Return (word,count) tuples in first normalized\noccurrence order. Do not use locale rules, NFKC or ASCII-only regexes. Empty or\nseparator-only input returns []. Input is a str; other input types raise TypeError.\nKeep every letter of scripts without spaces in the same word (no segmentation).\n\nCreate a plan, fully read words.py, run `python -m pytest -q` before first write;\nafter final write run the full same command, finish the plan and final_answer\nnormally once it passes. Standard library only; never edit tests.\n\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"generic\", \"editable\": [\"words.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"words.py\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 20}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\n\nCurrent plan; retain these exact titles and order, update status only:\n[{\"title\": \"Inspect repository and read words.py\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Implement Unicode-aware word_counts in words.py\", \"status\": \"doing\"}, {\"title\": \"Run full pytest and verify implementation\", \"status\": \"todo\"}]\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"finish_plan\",\"next_requirement\":\"Changes and current-file tests are complete. Mark the existing plan done, then final_answer.\",\"remaining_count\":1,\"requests_left\":12,\"baseline_done\":1,\"changed_files\":[\"words.py\"],\"verified_current\":1,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":8,\"max_requests\":20,\"requests_after_response\":12}"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\n\n```python\nresult = run_command(argv=[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"], cwd=\".\")\nprint(result)\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Latest execution feedback:\nExecutor output:\nExecution logs:\n{'argv': ['/mnt/d/Muiti-Agent Programing/experiments/code-agent-smolagents/24371220/.venv/bin/python', '-m', 'pytest', '-q'], 'cwd': '/home/ventsdenye/.local/state/code-agent/evaluations/additional-unicode_words-02-ogjtgu1g/repo', 'rc': 0, 'stdout': '...                                                                      [100%]\\n3 passed in 0.01s\\n', 'stderr': '', 'timed_out': False}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone\nRecent project tool results:\n[{\"tool\":\"write_file\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{\"path\":\"words.py\",\"file_hash\":\"cfb9a0fe1231bb3bd87e581c1b36d536af4d2428651fd332c68923a401962f1f\",\"changed\":true}},{\"tool\":\"update_plan\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{}},{\"tool\":\"read_file\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{\"path\"